data.content:
Output is `{"name":"Jane","age":30}` ✅

Here's the key part:

```csharp
var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
{
    PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase
};
JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
```

`JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase` converts PascalCase properties (`Name`, `Age`) to camelCase (`name`, `age`). Both `System.Text.Json` and the `CamelCase` policy are built into .NET 8 — no extra NuGet packages needed.
